{"name":"Light Pelican Bill","hex":"#e1ced4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"pelican","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various seabirds of the family Pelecanidae, having a long bill with a distendable pouch.","A native or resident of the American state of Louisiana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pelican"},{"term":"bill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A written list or inventory. (Now obsolete except in specific senses or set phrases; bill of lading, bill of goods, etc.)","A document, originally sealed; a formal statement or official memorandum. (Now obsolete except with certain qualifying words; bill of health, bill of sale etc.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To advertise by a bill or public notice.","To charge; to send a bill to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pelican","blocks":[{"text":"Pelicans are a genus of large water birds that make up the family Pelecanidae. They are characterized by a long beak and a large throat pouch used for catching prey and draining water from the scooped-up contents before swallowing. They have predominantly pale plumage, except for the brown and Peruvian pelicans. The bills, pouches, and bare facial skin of all pelicans become brightly coloured before the breeding season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg/330px-Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thum